Not exactly. Wireshark and Nmap perform different cybersecurity functions. They complement each other rather than replace each other.

### 1\. Wireshark vs Nmap

| Function                      | Wireshark | Nmap                     |
| ----------------------------- | --------- | ------------------------ |
| Capture network packets       | Yes       | Limited                  |
| Analyse network traffic       | Yes       | No, not its main purpose |
| Identify protocols            | Yes       | Some                     |
| Discover devices on a network | Limited   | Yes                      |
| Scan open ports               | No        | Yes                      |
| Identify running services     | No        | Yes                      |
| Detect operating systems      | No        | Yes                      |
| Inspect HTTP requests         | Yes       | Limited                  |
| Monitor network communication | Yes       | No, not continuously     |

